Having just broken through with a 13th level wizard, after many stupid
deaths I offer the following advice:


1) Until the wizard gets an AC around 0, he/she is quite vulnerable and
   normal barbaric assaults on low level monsters melee style is impossible
   and fatal.  Avoid all extended battles, especially with multiple 
   monsters or tough low level ones.  (I have died many times fighting
   dwarves one on one, especially with no attacking magic capabilities)
   This implies that a wizard must always look for ways of escaping nasty
   monsters.  All means of teleportation, even wizard locking a door
   between you and a number of monsters can help you survive the early
   levels.  Rest early and often, and use prayer if you're down to 
   less than 5 hit points and are just about to die.  Invisibility is a
   nice thing always in escape.

2) Always know what magic items you have and how you can use them.  If
   the wizard didn't start off with those items, he/she wouldn't have
   a chance.  Read your spellbooks around level 3 (your int should be
   good enough), and don't be afraid to use these spells often.  If
   your nerves tingle when casting a spell, you can refresh your knowledge
   of a spell by reading the spellbook again.  Wands must be identified
   very early (I always zap them soon after I get them), and a good 
   wand of striking can turn the tide of battle dramatically.

3) The wizard is not as well equipped with armor, so I have found it 
   necessary to rob shops unless I can train my pet.  Do this using
   teleportation (it no longer works to zap a wand at a pile of stuff),
   which means to teleport oneself out of a shop after gathering items
   that you want (nearly everything).  I'd say that I can avoid the
   Keystone Kops around 80-90% of the time until I bail the level, in
   the meantime being able to shore up quite a few nice items in the
   process.  Make sure you clear the level beforehand, and don't rob
   the shops in the Gnomish Mines because there are a lot of mean 
   guards down there.  Once again, you'll have to perfect your ways
   of bailing a level without getting trapped by the Kops.

4) SUMMARY: Be chicken.  Don't fight a battle that you won't dominate.
   Use magic early and often.  Upgrade your weapons and armor in every
   way, shape and form.

